head_commit.message:
libc++ static linking

xla/tsl/profiler/convert/oss/xla_op_utils.cc:24:29: error: 'constinit' specifier missing on initializing declaration of 'kHloSparseCoreV0Infeed' [-Werror,-Wmissing-constinit]
In C++20 mode (__cpp_constinit >= 201907L), ABSL_CONST_INIT expands to the C++20 constinit keyword. When a variable is declared constinit extern const in xla_op_utils.h, C++20 requires constinit (TF_CONST_INIT const) on the initializing definition as well (-Werror,-Wmissing-constinit).

Patches:
third_party/xla/third_party/cudnn_frontend_header_fix.patch
In libc++, std::mutex and std::lock_guard are annotated with Clang thread-safety attributes (_LIBCPP_THREAD_SAFETY_ANNOTATION(capability("mutex")), acquire_capability, release_capability), whereas libstdc++'s std::mutex is not.

In cudnn-frontend (include/cudnn_frontend_Heuristics.h), EngineHeuristicsBuilder_v8::build() conditionally locks and unlocks EngineHeuristics_v8::get_heur_b_mutex() across separate if statements:

cpp
if (m_heuristics.mode == CUDNN_HEUR_MODE_B) {
    EngineHeuristics_v8::get_heur_b_mutex().lock();
}
// Finalizing the descriptor
status = detail::finalize(m_heuristics.pointer->get_backend_descriptor());
if (m_heuristics.mode == CUDNN_HEUR_MODE_B) {
    EngineHeuristics_v8::get_heur_b_mutex().unlock();
}

Under -Werror -Wthread-safety-analysis, Clang rejects this pattern because the mutex is only held on one branch entering detail::finalize(...) and is then unlocked conditionally.

